  "last_message": "I added a new page, `docs/features/pickup-reminders.md`, and listed it in `docs/features/README.md`. Nothing is committed yet.\n\nThe page explains why reminders go by SMS, using what `notes/issue-52.md` records:\n- **The email trial:** reminders went by email from April to June 2025.\n- **What happened:** 34% of the reminder emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Each missed pickup means a packed bag whose fresh food is thrown away at closing time.\n- **Why SMS works:** many members share one family phone and rarely check email, but they see an SMS.\n- **The switch back:** SMS returned on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. Issue 52 was closed keeping SMS.\n- **For the next proposal:** it has to answer the unopened reminders and the wasted food, not just the 40 euros a month it would save.\n\nA short \"How it works\" section notes that the channel is the `CHANNEL` constant in `larder/reminders.py`.\n\nI made this a feature page rather than a decision record. The docs guide keeps decision records for choices that affect more than one feature or module, and this one is a single constant in one file. The page links to `notes/issue-52.md` as its source.",
